rows=[(231, 'the-pink-braid-between-us', 'The pink braid between us', 'Two middle-aged sisters quietly comb a doll, against expectations about who may play. Focus on the shared object of care, preserving its unusual pink hair and clothes without inventing the sisters or claiming a human likeness.', 'Horizontal 3:2 intimate colored-pencil drawing with light gouache. Close crop of a fictional fashion doll lying on a plain pale cloth, viewed obliquely from behind her head so no face or human likeness is shown. Her long clearly synthetic hot-pink hair falls across the cloth; part has been loosely braided with one narrow satin ribbon, remaining strands uneven. A tiny plain comb lies beside the hair, its teeth coherent and no hand holding it. A cropped turquoise fabric top and small edge of a subtly glittering skirt identify a toy torso at upper right. No actual person, no extra dolls, no branding, words or toy packaging. Quiet soft indoor light; care and unhurried play, not sentimental nursery decoration. Leave a generous quiet cloth area on the left.'), (234, 'milk-opened-at-dusk', 'Milk opened at dusk', 'The second haiku finds settling dusk in a tea seller opening a milk packet. An unstaged close counter fragment lets a modest action imply the wider working evening; it illustrates one haiku, not all ten.', 'Horizontal 3:2 soft dry pastel and graphite editorial still life at dusk: a small tea-stall counter seen at counter height, a plain unbranded soft milk pouch stands leaning securely against the side of a simple stainless steel saucepan, its upper corner freshly snipped open. Pouch weight and base folds plausible, no floating liquid or pouring. Saucepan rests flat on a modest unlit surface, no handle cutting through pouch. Cool dim evening ambience and a little warm light from an off-frame practical bulb, shadows locally consistent. Empty blurred plain background, no seller, hands, labels, text, menu, staged cups, decorative steam or market spectacle. Focus selective at the clipped pouch corner and one dull rim highlight, edges elsewhere soft.'), (238, 'a-few-seeds-to-share', 'A few seeds to share', 'The speaker brings home pieces of nature and shares them. A small open cloth bag with a few seeds suggests generosity and playful collecting without literally packaging stars, sunlight and all the poem’s nouns.', 'Horizontal 3:2 spare gouache and graphite study on opaque pale paper. A modest plain cotton drawstring bag rests open on its side toward the lower left of a simple tabletop; a few differently angled brown seeds are visible just inside its opening and two have slipped onto the surface beside it. Cloth folds shaped by its own weight and small contents, no stuffed luxury styling, no decorative embroidery, no labels or lettering. A short drawcord lies casually without perfect loop. One muted green edge of a blade of grass appears inside bag but does not make a bouquet. Most of right half quiet cream surface. Soft neutral daylight, contact shadows under bag/seeds only; no stars, fairy wings, literal parcel box, hands, people or extra props.')]
items=[]
